WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.966
Easy Folk Tales. Jack and the Beanstalk.

00:00:02.966 --> 00:00:05.702
Jack lived with his mother in a small house.

00:00:05.702 --> 00:00:07.071
They were very poor.

00:00:07.071 --> 00:00:09.124
All they had was one old cow.

00:00:09.124 --> 00:00:13.842
One day his mother said, "Jack, take the cow to the market and sell her."

00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:16.804
On the road, Jack met a strange old man.

00:00:16.804 --> 00:00:20.875
"I will give you five magic beans for your cow," said the man.

00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:24.757
Jack thought that was wonderful, and he took the beans home.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.721
His mother was very angry.

00:00:26.721 --> 00:00:29.471
"Five beans for a cow!" she cried.

00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:33.830
She threw the beans out of the window, and they went to bed with no dinner.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.249
In the morning Jack looked out of the window.

00:00:36.249 --> 00:00:38.989
A huge beanstalk had grown up in the night.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:41.235
It went up and up into the clouds.

00:00:41.235 --> 00:00:42.789
Jack began to climb.

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:47.843
At the top he found a road, and at the end of the road stood a very big house.

00:00:47.843 --> 00:00:49.271
A giant lived there.

00:00:49.271 --> 00:00:51.705
Jack hid behind a door and watched.

00:00:51.705 --> 00:00:54.151
The giant sat at the table with a hen.

00:00:54.151 --> 00:00:58.251
"Lay!" said the giant, and the hen laid a golden egg.

00:00:58.251 --> 00:01:00.218
Then the giant fell asleep.

00:01:00.218 --> 00:01:02.922
Jack took the hen under his arm and ran.

00:01:02.922 --> 00:01:06.314
But the hen made a noise, and the giant woke up.

00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:10.612
"Stop, thief!" he shouted, and he ran after Jack.

00:01:10.612 --> 00:01:13.782
Jack climbed down the beanstalk as fast as he could.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:16.387
The giant began to climb down after him.

00:01:16.387 --> 00:01:18.289
"Mother, bring the axe!"

00:01:18.289 --> 00:01:19.418
Jack shouted.

00:01:19.418 --> 00:01:22.113
He took the axe and cut through the beanstalk.

00:01:22.113 --> 00:01:26.637
It fell to the ground with a great noise, and that was the end of the giant.

00:01:26.637 --> 00:01:29.107
The hen laid a golden egg every day.

00:01:29.107 --> 00:01:31.871
Jack and his mother were never hungry again.
